## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical stateful streaming concepts: windowed aggregations, per-tenant isolation, watermark-based late data handling, and exactly-once guarantees across rebalances. It also tests testing discipline and observability planning.

## Key Concepts

- Stateful windowed aggregations with per-(tenantId, userId) keys
- Watermarks and late-arrival handling (120s)
- Reb alo nce-safe state partitioning and eviction
- Exactly-once or idempotent sinks with proper offsets
- Observability and test strategy for late data and rebalancing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton: window state store and onEvent flow
class WindowAggregator {
  constructor(windowMs, watermarkMs) { /* init stores */ }
  onEvent(e) {
    // e = {tenantId, userId, ts, value}
    const ws = Math.floor(e.ts / this.windowMs) * this.windowMs;
    const key = `${e.tenantId}:${e.userId}:${ws}`;
    let bucket = this.state.get(key) || {sum: 0, count: 0, maxTs: 0};
    bucket.sum += e.value;
    bucket.count += 1;
    bucket.maxTs = Math.max(bucket.maxTs, e.ts);
    this.state.set(key, bucket);
    // emit when window closes or on a timer
  }
}
```

